# Day 33

## Experiment Title

Understanding Maven Project Structure and POM File


## Objective

To study the structure of a Maven project and understand the purpose of the pom.xml file.


## Theory

A Maven project follows a standard directory structure which helps developers organize source code, test files, resources, and build outputs efficiently.

The pom.xml file is the core configuration file of a Maven project. It contains project details, dependencies, plugins, build configurations, and version information. Maven uses this file to manage the complete build lifecycle of the application.


## Requirements

Java Development Kit

Apache Maven

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Maven project directory.

Study the standard folder structure of the Maven project.

Locate and open the pom.xml configuration file.

Observe project information, dependencies, and plugin configurations.

Understand how Maven manages the project using the pom.xml file.


## Output

The Maven project structure was studied successfully.

The pom.xml file was analyzed successfully.

Project dependencies and build configurations were understood properly.


## Result

Successfully understood the Maven project structure and the role of the pom.xml configuration file.
